# Semantic commit messages

All commits must follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):

```
<type>(optional-scope): <short summary>
```

## Types

| Type | Use when |
|------|----------|
| `feat` | New user-facing capability |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `refactor` | Code change with no behavior change |
| `chore` | Tooling, deps, config, housekeeping |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `test` | Tests only |
| `build` | Build system or dependency upgrades that affect the build |
| `ci` | CI configuration |
| `style` | Formatting only (no logic change) |
| `revert` | Revert a previous commit |

## Rules

- Summary in **imperative mood**, lowercase after the type (e.g. `fix: correct date binding`)
- Keep the subject **≤ ~72 characters**; no trailing period
- Prefer a scope when helpful: `fix(auth):`, `chore(deps):`, `feat(alerts):`
- Use `chore(deps):` for Dependabot / security dependency bumps
- Body optional; use it for *why*, breaking changes, or issue refs (`Closes #123`)
- **One logical change per commit** when practical; security bumps may be a single `chore(deps):` commit

## Examples

```
feat(alerts): group home signals by sector
fix(cron): skip duplicate EOD rows for the same trade date
chore(deps): upgrade next and remove vulnerable packages
docs: add Vercel cutover checklist
```

## Avoid

```
Fixed stuff
Update
WIP
feat: Added new feature.  # past tense + period
```
